{"ref":"BDB, עָשׁ³","hw":"עָשׁ³","html":"† II. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">עָשׁ</span></big>  <strong>n.m.</strong><sup><a data-ref=\"Isaiah 50:9\" href=\"/Isaiah.50.9\">Is 50:9</a></sup> <strong>moth (</strong>as <em>waster, consumer</em><strong>)</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳</span> abs., <a data-ref=\"Hosea 5:12\" href=\"/Hosea.5.12\">Ho 5:12</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">רָקָב</span>), <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 50:9\" href=\"/Isaiah.50.9\">Is 50:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 51:8\" href=\"/Isaiah.51.8\">51:8</a>; in sim. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 39:12\" href=\"/Psalms.39.12\">ψ 39:12</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">כְּבֶגֶד אֲכָלוֹ עָשׁ</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 13:28\" href=\"/Job.13.28\">Jb 13:28</a>; symbol of fragility <a data-ref=\"Job 4:19\" href=\"/Job.4.19\">Jb 4:19</a>.—<a data-ref=\"Job 27:18\" href=\"/Job.27.18\">27:18</a> read prob. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַכָּבִישׁ</span> q.v.","next":"BDB, עָשַׁת","prev":"BDB, עָשֵׁשׁ"}